 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Device and uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "One N-channel enhancement power MOSFET of Infineon's OptiMOS 5 line, rated 100 V, normal gate level, in the TOLL package (PG-HSOF-8). It is meant for fast switching and synchronous rectification, with a low figure of merit of gate charge times RDS(on). Every unit is avalanche tested. Leads are lead-free plated, RoHS compliant, halogen-free to IEC 61249-2-21, and qualification follows JEDEC (J-STD20 and JESD22) for the target applications."
  },
  {
   "topic": "On-resistance and gate drive",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "At 10 V of gate drive and 150 A, RDS(on) is 1.3 mΩ typical and 1.5 mΩ max; with 6 V and 75 A it is 1.6 mΩ typical and 2.0 mΩ max. Threshold lies between 2.2 and 3.8 V at 280 µA. In Diagram 6 the resistance at 10 V stays near 1.3 mΩ out to 800 A, while at 5 V and 5.5 V it climbs sharply past roughly 230 A and 490 A. Diagram 9 shows RDS(on) at 10 V and 150 A going from about 1.3 mΩ at 25 °C to about 2.6 mΩ typical, 3.2 mΩ max at 175 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gate charge",
   "page": 9,
   "text": "On a plot of VGS against gate charge: Qg(th) runs from zero up to the threshold voltage; Qgs runs from zero to where the Miller plateau starts; Qgd covers the plateau; Qsw runs from the threshold to the end of the plateau; Qg is the whole charge up to the final gate voltage. At 50 V, 100 A and 0 to 10 V these are 36, 53, 34, 51 and 169 nC typical, and the plateau sits at 4.4 V. For the sync. FET case, with VDS at 0.1 V, the total is 146 nC."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current ratings and temperature",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The 353 A, 250 A and 35 A continuous ratings apply to the part alone with the case (or ambient, for 35 A) at the stated temperature; Diagram 2 traces the allowed current from 353 A flat to 25 °C case down to zero at 175 °C, and Diagram 1 the dissipation from 375 W at 25 °C to zero at 175 °C. Pulsed drain and diode current are both 1412 A."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Avalanche",
   "page": 9,
   "text": "Single-pulse avalanche energy is 775 mJ at 150 A with 25 Ω gate-source resistance. Diagram 13 gives the avalanche current that can be carried against its duration for starting junction temperatures of 25, 100 and 150 °C, all capped at 150 A for short times."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Production test",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Gate resistance, the three capacitances, Qgd, Qg, Qoss, trr and Qrr are set by design and not tested in production."
  }
 ],
